# Cloud Compliance Auditor on AWS

A production-oriented, serverless cloud security auditing solution built on AWS to automatically assess infrastructure compliance, generate reports, and trigger alerts.

---

## Summary

Cloud Compliance Auditor is a serverless security assessment framework designed to evaluate AWS infrastructure against foundational security best practices.

The solution automatically:

- Scans IAM configurations
- Audits EC2 security groups
- Validates EBS encryption settings
- Generates structured compliance reports
- Stores reports in Amazon S3
- Sends alert notifications via Amazon SNS

---

## Business Objective

The objective of this project is to automate cloud security validation and reduce manual audit effort.

The system ensures early detection of misconfigurations such as:

- Publicly exposed ports
- Unencrypted storage volumes
- Missing MFA enforcement

This minimizes security risk and improves governance posture.

---

## System Architecture Overview

The solution follows a fully serverless, event-driven architecture:

- **AWS Lambda** – Core compliance scanning engine (Python + boto3)
- **Amazon EventBridge** – Scheduled execution (cron-based trigger)
- **Amazon S3** – Secure storage for compliance reports
- **Amazon SNS** – Real-time alert notifications
- **AWS IAM** – Least-privilege role-based access control
- **Amazon CloudWatch Logs** – Execution logging and debugging

---

## Functional Capabilities

### Security Group Exposure Detection
- Detects ports 22 (SSH) and 3389 (RDP) open to `0.0.0.0/0`

### EBS Encryption Validation
- Identifies unencrypted volumes

### IAM MFA Enforcement
- Flags IAM users without MFA enabled

### Automated Report Generation
- Timestamped text-based compliance report
- Stored securely in S3

### Real-Time Alerts
- SNS notifications triggered when findings exist

### Scheduled Execution
- Fully automated using EventBridge cron rules

---

## Security & Governance Controls

- Principle of Least Privilege applied to Lambda execution role
- IAM role-based authentication (no hardcoded credentials)
- Encrypted data at rest in S3
- Event-driven architecture reducing attack surface
- Structured severity-based findings classification

---

## SDLC Methodology Followed

- **Requirement Analysis** – Defined compliance scope and detection logic
- **System Design** – Designed event-driven serverless architecture
- **Implementation** – Developed compliance engine in Python using boto3
- **Testing** – Validated detection logic with controlled misconfigurations
- **Deployment** – Configured IAM roles and AWS services via Console
- **Monitoring & Optimization** – Used CloudWatch Logs for debugging and performance tuning

